---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import styles from '../pages-styles/about.module.scss';
import { urlWithBaseUrl } from '@utils/urlWithBaseUrl';
---

<Layout
    title="Niall Crosby: Our Amazing Founder"
    description="The story and legacy of Niall Crosby, founder of AG Grid."
    showSearchBar={true}
    showDocsNav={false}
>
    <div class="layout-max-width-small">
        <section class={styles.introSection}>
            <h2>Our Amazing Founder</h2>
            <p>
                We are proud to be the leading Javascript datagrid on the market, with thousands of customers globally.
                Our ethos and culture derive from the creative force of one person. Our founder Niall Crosby.
            </p>
        </section>

        <div class={styles.headerSection}>
            <img src={urlWithBaseUrl('images/niall.jpg')} alt="Photo of Niall Crosby" class={styles.nialHeaderImage} />
            <span>Niall Crosby 1977-2024</span>
        </div>

        <section class={styles.contentSection}>
            <div class={styles.niallSectionContent}>
                <div class={styles.niallTextBlock}>
                    <p>
                        A lover of tech, travel and adventure, Niall was a fiercely independent thinker. He had been
                        coding since a young age and delighted in seeing patterns, trends and solutions that others
                        could not.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        He had an enormous curiosity for how things work, and this drove him fearlessly and
                        entrepreneurially into the world of software development.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        While working as a freelance developer around 2014 / 2015, Niall felt a deep frustration with
                        what was available in the market to handle large data sets in browser-based applications. He
                        decided to do something about it.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        What he developed was so functional, reliable, stable – an apparently simple solution to a
                        fiendishly complex issue. Niall recognised that what he had created didn’t just sort his problem
                        – it had the potential to scale and solve the problems of companies throughout the world.
                    </p>
                    <p>This was the beginning of AG Grid.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class={styles.contentSection}>
            <div class={styles.niallSectionContent}>
                <div class={styles.niallTextBlock}>
                    <p>Niall sadly lost his life in a helicopter crash in July 2024 in his native Ireland.</p>
                    <p>
                        His legacy however lives on in the ambition and creativity he instilled in everyone at AG Grid.
                        It is evident in the inspiration and generous support he provided to countless young developers
                        and start-ups throughout his career.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        And it lives on in the memories of his friends and his young family who were central to his
                        life.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        At AG Grid we are proud to continue that legacy. Many of us have been on the journey with Niall
                        since the start.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        As Niall’s friends and work family we are committed to pushing the boundaries of Javascript
                        datagrids, constantly developing new features and products to show the world what is possible.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        AG Grid is about fearlessly tackling big challenges, supporting our clients, inspiring each
                        other and having fun along the way – attributes Niall was a big believer in.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>
    </div>
</Layout>
